{"text": "Communication has two sides.\n\nReceptive is how he takes information in.\n\nWhen he is well, he understands Grade 10 language easily. When he is tired or unwell, he understands less.\n\nSo use short, calm sentences. One instruction at a time. Write it down as well as saying it.\n\nGive him time to answer.\n\nNo jokes or sarcasm when he is upset. He can take them the wrong way.\n\nExpressive is how he tells us what he needs.\n\nHe talks and he writes. Writing is usually clearer for him.\n\nHe uses a scale from 1 to 5. One means he needs to leave now. Five means he is doing well.\n\nHe uses a break card. When it goes on his desk, say yes straight away.\n\nWhen he is low he says very little. When he is high he talks fast.\n\nSpeak to Liam, not about him. Do not speak for him.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "category-h-slide-04.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Communication", "start": 0.1, "end": 1.05, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 13}, {"text": "has", "start": 1.0625, "end": 1.3125, "start_char": 14, "end_char": 17}, {"text": "two", "start": 1.325, "end": 1.5375, "start_char": 18, "end_char": 21}, {"text": "sides", "start": 1.55, "end": 2.2, "start_char": 22, "end_char": 27}, {"text": "Receptive", "start": 2.6, "end": 3.3375, "start_char": 30, "end_char": 39}, {"text": "is", "start": 3.35, "end": 3.5375, "start_char": 40, "end_char": 42}, {"text": "how", "start": 3.55, "end": 3.7375, "start_char": 43, "end_char": 46}, {"text": "he", "start": 3.75, "end": 3.9, "start_char": 47, "end_char": 49}, {"text": "takes", "start": 3.9125, "end": 4.2375, "start_char": 50, "end_char": 55}, {"text": "information", "start": 4.25, "end": 4.875, "start_char": 56, "end_char": 67}, {"text": "in", "start": 4.8875, "end": 5.175, "start_char": 68, "end_char": 70}, {"text": "When", "start": 5.575, "end": 5.7625, "start_char": 73, "end_char": 77}, {"text": "he", "start": 5.775, "end": 5.925, "start_char": 78, "end_char": 80}, {"text": "is", "start": 5.9375, "end": 6.075, "start_c